71096400, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/63569754", "supplied_md5": "431c3ab781a586035739b5930234bafe", "computed_md5": "431c3ab781a586035739b5930234bafe", "mimetype": "application/octet-stream"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 23480557, "full_name": "Weiyu Chen", "first_name": "Weiyu", "last_name": "Chen", "is_active": true, "url_name": "Weiyu_Chen", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://janelia.figshare.com/articles/dataset/_b_Whole-brain_all-optical_interrogation_of_neuronal_dynamics_underlying_gut_and_vascular_interoception_in_zebrafish_b_/31967640", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\">Weiyu Chen<sup>1,</sup>*, Ben James<sup>1,2,</sup>*, Virginie M. S. Ruetten<sup>1,</sup>*, Sambashiva Banala<sup>1</sup>, Ziqiang Wei<sup>1</sup>, Xueying Yang<sup>1</sup>, Greg Fleishman<sup>1</sup>, Mikail Rubinov<sup>3</sup>, Jeremy Delahanty<sup>1</sup>,Mark C. Fishman<sup>4</sup>, Florian Engert<sup>5</sup>, Luke D. Lavis<sup>1</sup>, James E. Fitzgerald<sup>1,2,6,#</sup>, Misha B. Ahrens<sup>1,#</sup></p><p dir=\"ltr\">1.Janelia Research Campus, Howard Hughes Medical Institute, Ashburn, VA, USA.<sup> </sup>2.<sup> </sup>Department of Neurobiology, Northwestern University, Evanston, IL, USA. 3. Department of Biomedical Engineering, Vanderbilt, Nashville, TN, USA.<sup> </sup>4. Harvard Stem Cell Institute, Harvard University, Cambridge, MA, USA.<sup> </sup>5. Department of Molecular and Cellular Biology, Harvard University, Cambridge, MA, USA.<sup> </sup>6. NSF-Simons National Institute for Theory and Mathematics in Biology, Chicago, IL, USA. *<sup> </sup>Equal first-author contribution, <sup>#</sup><sup> </sup>equal senior-author contribution.</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b>Abstract</b></p><p dir=\"ltr\">Internal signals from the body and external signals from the environment are processed by brain-wide circuits to guide behavior. However, the complete brain-wide circuit activity underlying interoception, the sensation and perception of bodily signals, and its interactions with sensorimotor circuits remain unclear due to technical barriers to accessing whole-brain activity at the cellular level during organ physiology perturbations. We developed an all-optical system for whole-brain neuronal imaging in behaving larval zebrafish during optical uncaging of gut- or vasculature-targeted nutrients and visuo-motor stimulation. Widespread neural activity throughout the brain encoded nutrient delivery, unfolding on multiple timescales across many specific peripheral and central regions. Evoked activity depended on delivery location and occurred with the amino acids glutamate and D-glucose, but not L-glucose. Many gut-sensitive neurons also responded to swimming and visual stimuli, with brainstem areas primarily integrating gut and motor signals and midbrain regions integrating gut visual, and motor signals. This platform links body-brain communication studies to brain-wide neural computation in awake, behaving vertebrates.</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b>1. Volumetric Imaging Data</b></p><p dir=\"ltr\">The imaging datasets were processed and generated using the<a href=\"https://github.com/mikarubi/voluseg?tab=readme-ov-file\" target=\"_blank\"> <u>Volumetric Segmentation Pipeline (Voluseg)</u></a>.</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b>cells0_clean.hdf5:</b></p><ul><li><b>background</b>: estimated background fluorescence.</li><li><b>cell_baseline</b>: computed cell baselines.</li><li><b>cell_timeseries</b>: detrended [+ optionally filtered] cell timeseries.</li><li><b>cell_timeseries_raw</b>: raw cell timeseries (direct output of segmentation).</li><li><b>cell_weights</b>: cell spatial footprints (spatial NMF components).</li><li><b>cell_x/y/z</b>: cell coordinates.</li><li><b>n/t</b>: number of cells/timepoints.</li><li><b>volume_id</b>: cell ids represented on a volume.</li><li><b>volume_weight</b>: cell spatial footprints represented on a volume.</li><li><b>x/y/z</b>: volume dimensions.</li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><b>volume0.hdf5:</b></p><ul><li><b>background</b>: estimated background fluorescence.</li><li><b>block_valids</b>: indices of blocks used for segmentation.</li><li><b>block_xyz0/1</b>: min/max block xyz coordinates.</li><li><b>n_blocks</b>: total number of blocks.</li><li><b>n_voxels_cells</b>: approximate number of voxels in each cell.</li><li><b>thr_intensity</b>: brain-mask intensity threshold.</li><li><b>thr_probability</b>: brain-mask probability threshold.</li><li><b>volume_mean/mask/peak</b>: volume mean/mask/local peak intensity.</li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><b>2. Electrophysiology and Stimulus Metadata</b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b>eP.26chFlt-v10</b> contains the fictive swimming recordings, camera triggers, and stimulus parameters. To generate the associated metadata, you will need to use the eclass.py script from this GitHub repository: https://github.com/benJames1212/gutBrainPipeline.</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b>Key Channels:</b></p><ul><li><b>sr</b>: Acquisition sampling rate (Hz).</li><li><b>ch_ep0</b>: Left channel recording of the fictive swim signal.</li><li><b>ch_ep1</b>: Right channel recording of the fictive swim signal.</li><li><b>ch_LS0</b>: Light-sheet acquisition trigger for the green fluorescence channel.</li><li><b>ch_LS1</b>: Light-sheet acquisition trigger for the red fluorescence channel.</li><li><b>ch_uvtrial</b>: Trigger signal indicating the onset of the ultraviolet (UV) stimulus.</li><li><b>ch_gpos</b>: Spatial coordinate tracking the position of the UV stimulus.</li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><b>ch_velmul</b>: Velocity parameter of the applied visual grating stimulus.</p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 250624928820, "created_date": "2026-04-13T22:45:47Z", "modified_date": "2026-04-13T22:45:47Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["zebrafish", "whole-brain imaging", "optical uncaging", "gut-brain axis", "blood glucose", "interoception"], "keywords": ["zebrafish", "whole-brain imaging", "optical uncaging", "gut-brain axis", "blood glucose", "interoception"], "categories": [{"id": 24415, "title": "Animal neurobiology", "parent_id": 24397, "path": "/24130/24397/24415", "source_id": "310906", "taxonomy_id": 100}, {"id": 30331, "title": "Behavioural neuroscience", "parent_id": 30325, "path": "/30292/30325/30331", "source_id": "520202", "taxonomy_id": 100}, {"id": 24736, "title": "Computational neuroscience (incl. mathematical neuroscience and theoretical neuroscience)", "parent_id": 24724, "path": "/24457/24724/24736", "source_id": "320904", "taxonomy_id": 100}], "references": [], "has_linked_file": false, "citation": "Chen, Weiyu (2026). Whole-brain, all-optical interrogation of neuronal dynamics underlying gut and vascular interoception in zebrafish. Janelia Research Campus. Dataset. https://doi.org/10.25378/janelia.31967640.v1", "related_materials": [], "is_embargoed": false, "embargo_date": null, "embargo_type": null, "embargo_title": "", "embargo_reason": "", "embargo_options": [], "id": 31967640, "title": "<b>Whole-brain, all-optical interrogation of neuronal dynamics underlying gut and vascular interoception in zebrafish</b>", "doi": "10.25378/janelia.31967640.v1", "handle": "", "url": "https://api.figshare.com/v2/articles/31967640", "published_date": "2026-04-13T22:45:47Z", "thumb": "", "defined_type": 3, "defined_type_name": "dataset", "group_id": 11380, "url_private_api": "https://api.figshare.com/v2/account/articles/31967640", "url_public_api": "https://api.figshare.com/v2/articles/31967640", "url_private_html": "https://figshare.com/account/articles/31967640", "url_public_html": "https://janelia.figshare.com/articles/dataset/_b_Whole-brain_all-optical_interrogation_of_neuronal_dynamics_underlying_gut_and